.TH FERRI 1 "@DATE@" "Ferri @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferri \- install Android and iOS apps on connected devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferri \-\-target
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-device " ID"]
.br
.B ferri \-\-url
.I URL
.RB [ \-\-android " | " \-\-ios ]
.RB [ \-\-device " ID"]
.br
.B ferri \-\-list
.br
.B ferri \-\-help
.br
.B ferri version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ferri is a cross-platform app installation tool for app testers and
developers.
It installs local APK, APKS, AAB and IPA packages, or downloads packages from
URLs.
.PP
With multiple compatible devices, Ferri asks you to select a device and
confirm.
Non-interactive sessions must select a device with
.B \-\-device
when more than one compatible device is connected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-target " PATH"
Install a local APK, APKS, AAB or IPA package. Quote paths containing spaces.
.TP
.B \-\-url URL
Download a direct package URL or resolve a supported installation page.
Public Pgyer pages and combined Android/iOS pages are supported.
Combined pages may require a platform selection.
Google Play links open the store on the Android device; they do not download
an APK.
App Store links cannot be used to obtain an IPA directly.
Not all third-party pages can be resolved; use a direct package URL if
necessary.
.TP
.B \-\-android
Select Android for a URL installation.
.TP
.B \-\-ios
Select iOS for a URL installation.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " ID"
Install on the device with this exact ID. Use with target or URL installation.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List connected Android and iOS devices.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version ", " version
Show the version, release date and repository URL.
.SH INSTALLATION AND APP DATA
Ferri first attempts an update to preserve existing app data.
If installation fails and the same application ID or bundle ID is already
installed, Ferri can offer to uninstall it and retry.
Uninstalling deletes local app data and requires explicit confirmation.
Non-interactive sessions never confirm this destructive fallback
automatically.
.PP
Enable USB debugging on Android. Unlock and trust the computer on iOS.
For Android connection failures, Ferri may restart the adb server once and
retry
discovery. Device listing and completion do not restart the server.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Missing device tools are downloaded only after confirmation and stored under
.IR ~/.ferri .
Java and bundletool are needed only for AAB/APKS packages.
Help, version output and completion do not download tools.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ferri \-\-list
ferri \-\-target "build/My App.apk"
ferri \-\-target app.ipa \-\-device DEVICE_ID
ferri \-\-url https://example.com/app.apk \-\-android
ferri \-\-url https://www.pgyer.com/clobotics-rea-test \-\-android
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ferri
Managed device tools and supporting downloads.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1)
.PP
https://github.com/leo1394/homebrew-ferri
